<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mazaces</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 333–<a href="/years/331-bce">331 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mazaces was the last Persian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius III</a>. Appointed after his predecessor Sabaces fell at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-issus">Battle of Issus</a> in 333 BCE, he had no army able to resist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> and surrendered the country to him without a fight in 332 BCE, handing over Memphis and its treasury. Egypt then passed under Macedonian rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mazaces.jpg" alt="Mazaces" width="320" height="148" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PERSIA,_Alexandrine_Empire._Mazakes._Satrap_of_Mesopotamia,_331-323-2_BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
